1
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:16,917
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,897
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you!

7
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,637
So bright, so bold, and so elusive.

9
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,717
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,697
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:02,517
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem!

14
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:05,577
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see!

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,897
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:11,940
Believe in wonderland!

17
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,137
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
Live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,557
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,637
We don't want to live ordinary lives.

24
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:39,777
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,540
We live in one another.

26
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:58,757
And that's when it happened.

27
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:02,840
I looked him straight in the eye
and yelled, You bow-legged bastard!

28
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:05,280
And ever since that day,

29
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,837
crabs throughout the world have been
self-conscious about being bow-legged.

30
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:12,460
Oh, that's the reason
they walk sideways? Yep,

31
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:14,077
and at that pivotal moment,

32
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:18,042
a lobster happened to be within
earshot and heard the whole thing.

33
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:20,900
Oh, so lobsters are crabs too?

34
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:22,880
Better believe it. Oh.

35
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:26,417
Zoro, why don't you relax?

36
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:30,880
You're just wasting your energy
doing that who asked you excuse him.

37
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:32,020
No, he's hopeless

38
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:36,117
Guys like Zoro they got to keep
moving or they won't stay focused.

39
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:38,680
They have one-track minds especially

40
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:46,642
Our own resident muscle freak here now that
he's had a taste of the seven warlords?

41
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:51,137
Stop whining just say what's
on your mind or shut up!

42
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:53,280
Ah, you need me to spell it out?

43
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:56,397
All this tough guy bluster
is just a sad attempt

44
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:59,077
to mask your fear that
Luffy might lose this one.

45
00:02:59,160 --> 00:02:59,990
Who, me?

46
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:01,840
You saying I'm scared, huh?

47
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:03,277
Is that what you're saying?

48
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:05,980
Look at me, fancy eyebrows! That's it!

49
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:07,940
I've had enough of you!

50
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,620
You damn Mosshead!

51
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:10,958
What'd you call me?

52
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:12,720
You wanna go at it?

53
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,820
Cut it out! This is pointless!

54
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:19,600
Look at them!

55
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:21,277
They're at each other's throats!

56
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,437
Everyone's worked up!

57
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:27,220
It's up to me as Vice-Captain to
take charge! Calm down! All of you!

58
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:30,977
Everyone's frightened, yes, but
we mustn't turn on each other!

59
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:33,557
Luffy's cowering on us
to meet him in Alubarna!

60
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:36,464
Yeah, well, you see more
on eggs than any of us!

61
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:41,433
Keep your mind on the Rebellion
and leave the rest to us!

62
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,380
Sorry about that, Vivi.

63
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:46,684
If we tear each other
apart, we've already lost.

64
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:49,069
All right, that's settled.

65
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:51,777
Now let's devote our
attention to Elabarna.

66
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:53,095
Full speed, scissors!

67
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:57,150
Scissors?

68
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:59,040
Name for the crab. Oh.

69
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:00,717
You just baked that up.

70
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:01,897
Got something better?

71
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:02,862
No, not really.

72
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:13,450
Water!

73
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:15,920
I can hardly believe my eyes.

74
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:19,957
Precious water!

75
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:22,360
The water is coming forth!

76
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,397
Didn't I tell you, Luffy?

77
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:30,260
This land is strong!

78
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:35,520
Through it all, Yuba lives on!

79
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:44,160
This sandstorm will deal Yuba
a final destructive blow.

80
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:50,780
Banning the flames of anger within the
rebel army until an inferno ignites!

81
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:58,740
But in the end, the bleeding hearts which
infest this land are what's killing it.

82
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:03,537
And you, Straw Hat Luffy,
are the worst of them all?

83
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:06,940
If only you had purged
yourself of such weakness,

84
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:09,319
you may have lived a little longer.

85
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:11,990
Water.

86
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:17,280
I assume you don't feel so
indebted to this water now.

87
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,800
What's this?

88
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:33,640
You're still alive?

89
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:54,540
That looks like it hurts.

90
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:57,427
But you'll be out of
your misery soon enough.

91
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:06,830
Goodbye.

92
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:15,520
That was a complete waste of my time.

93
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:28,937
Not so bad.

94
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:31,217
Once we've weathered this storm!

95
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:33,777
The rain will bless us with sweet relief.

96
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:35,280
Just like always.

97
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:41,077
Your winds will never vanquish us!

98
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,537
You cowardly storm?

99
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:45,700
Yuba will never give in to the sand.

100
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:56,470
Me?

101
00:06:56,553 --> 00:06:57,700
Go to Alubarna?

102
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:01,289
Are we chasing after
the Straw Hat Pirates?

103
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,900
Or, uh, reinforcing the Royal Army?

104
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:05,140
That's up to you.

105
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:10,497
You'll have to decide which is
more important when you get there.

106
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:12,537
But, sir, I don't understand.

107
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:13,700
What's going on?

108
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:18,177
Rely on your sense of justice.

109
00:07:18,260 --> 00:07:21,460
Whatever happens, I'll
accept responsibility.

110
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,537
Captain, where are you going?

111
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:26,057
I have to head out to sea.

112
00:07:26,140 --> 00:07:27,757
Something unforeseen has come up.

113
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:31,077
Be on alert to receive
communication from me at any time.

114
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:31,990
Right.

115
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:36,776
I need you to keep a vigilant eye on
this country and where it ends up.

116
00:07:39,180 --> 00:07:41,533
Whether it falls or whether it survives,

117
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:45,211
the dawn of a brand new and
historic age is on the horizon.

118
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:54,497
Sergeant Major!

119
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:55,517
Sergeant Major!

120
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,080
Your orders! Yes.

121
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:02,373
Whether it falls or whether it survives,

122
00:08:02,620 --> 00:08:06,091
the dawn of a brand new and
historic age is on the horizon.

123
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:17,512
Our target is the pirate Straw Hat
Luffy and everyone who serves under him.

124
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:19,744
All hands, reinforce your gear.

125
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:22,400
Prepare to depart for Alubarna. Right!

126
00:08:24,260 --> 00:08:25,660
Straw Hat Luffy.

127
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:36,400
Damn you, Cobra.

128
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:39,117
My brethren and I are
willing to defend Alabasta

129
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:41,317
with every last drop
of blood in our bodies.

130
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:43,871
We will die before turning it over to you.

131
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:53,130
Hurry!

132
00:08:53,213 --> 00:08:54,043
Step lively!

133
00:08:54,126 --> 00:08:55,804
Stop dawdling around and focus!

134
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:58,099
We need more cannonballs over here!

135
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:02,310
Chaka!

136
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:06,915
The enemy's number is said
to be well over two million.

137
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:12,117
Tell me, soldier, what do you think
of His Majesty's attack on Nanohana?

138
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:16,435
I have served His Majesty for over
ten years, and I was quite surprised.

139
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:17,350
You're right.

140
00:09:17,433 --> 00:09:20,277
There's really no way
anyone could rationalize it.

141
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:23,595
Logic would suggest something
has happened to the king.

142
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:29,200
If true, it is all the more reason
why we must not lose this fight.

143
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:35,360
Bury your fear deep, for your king's
sake, as well as that of Princess Phoebe.

144
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:38,620
We will defend this country at all costs.

145
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:43,037
Everyone who is not prepared to
fight, take shelter outside the city.

146
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:46,517
We cannot guarantee your safety
if you would like to stay.

147
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:50,012
If we don't get out of here,
we'll be in the line of fire.

148
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:53,589
Banks are getting hectic
down there, I see.

149
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:56,037
But it's still moving too slow!

150
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:57,297
Hurry up and fight already!

151
00:09:57,380 --> 00:09:58,792
I can't see him waiting!

152
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:05,180
I can't take this!

153
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:07,337
I really don't care if
he is or isn't the king!

154
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:10,897
I've got to go out of my mind if I have
to stand here guarding him any longer!

155
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:11,837
Can't! Can't!

156
00:10:11,920 --> 00:10:12,920
Can't take this!

157
00:10:15,420 --> 00:10:16,300
I mean, sure,

158
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:19,357
slipping past the palace guards and
kidnapping this royal pain in the rear

159
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:22,137
is a mission which only a team of
our accomplished skills can pull off.

160
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:25,797
But now that it's over, this
assignment has become a tedious bore!

161
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:26,710
Right, Mr.

162
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:27,623
Four?

163
00:10:27,706 --> 00:10:30,757
Did anything I said manage to seep
through that thick head of yours?

164
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,075
Slow, you're so slow!

165
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:34,920
Ugh, my back is killing me!

166
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:38,100
Chaka, Koza, you mustn't fight.

167
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:41,735
The two of you embody the
spirit of this great country.

168
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:44,336
Divided, you only weaken her resolve.

169
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:48,500
There are those who lament war.

170
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:56,980
and those who race towards it.

171
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:06,700
Just go ahead and run away. Ooh.

172
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:12,720
Still, others incite war.

173
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:15,833
But for the very few who know the truth,

174
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:17,869
they strive to prevent it.

175
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:21,900
These widely opposing viewpoints
all have one thing in common.

176
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:26,580
They are about to clash here in
the capital city of Alubarna.

177
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:32,470
What?

178
00:11:32,553 --> 00:11:34,777
What do you mean we
can't cross this river?

179
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:35,742
Think about it.

180
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:37,537
Moving crabs are creatures of the desert.

181
00:11:37,620 --> 00:11:38,597
They don't take to water.

182
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:40,200
Has everyone gone nuts?

183
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,280
It's a crab!

184
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:43,780
They can exist on land and water!

185
00:11:44,420 --> 00:11:45,880
Guys, this is not good.

186
00:11:46,140 --> 00:11:47,397
This is a serious problem.

187
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:48,310
Look,

188
00:11:48,393 --> 00:11:50,777
if we just carelessly spend our
energy swimming across the river,

189
00:11:50,860 --> 00:11:52,437
We're not gonna make it in time.

190
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:53,977
See here after the river.

191
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:56,257
There's tons of desert to deal with So if

192
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:58,037
this crab can't make
it to the other shore,

193
00:11:58,120 --> 00:12:00,537
are we supposed to run the
rest of the way on foot?

194
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:01,817
We don't have a choice.

195
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:03,371
We won't make it in time.

196
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:05,480
It's absolutely impossible

197
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:17,720
Hey, I can see it Sandora
River straight ahead. Oh great.

198
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:21,060
Help us scissors pretty please I know!

199
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,120
Scissors loves dancer girls!

200
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:27,280
Will this do? Probably.

201
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:29,260
Whoa, I can't take it!

202
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:33,340
He's looking this way!

203
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:37,220
We're accelerating!

204
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,040
Bobby's won!

205
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:45,912
Great, now we've got two animals in heat!

206
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:47,620
Alright, we're moving now!

207
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:52,620
And what exactly has this
solved, Chopper? Nothing!

208
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:00,400
Go faster!

209
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,077
I'm seeing it, but I don't believe it.

210
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:09,572
This crab is incredible.

211
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:11,380
Way to go!

212
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:14,094
Now don't you stop, just keep on going!

213
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:16,440
Hurry, run, run, run all the way!

214
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:17,790
Go!

215
00:13:17,873 --> 00:13:18,703
Keep moving!

216
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:20,097
Nothing can stop us now!

217
00:13:20,180 --> 00:13:21,317
Oh, I love this crab!

218
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:23,220
Hey, what's going on?

219
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:26,262
If I didn't know better,
I think we were sinking!

220
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:33,740
You stupid crab! It's over.

221
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,357
No use whining about it.

222
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,270
Keep moving.

223
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:37,840
Hold on a second.

224
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:40,077
Are you sure there are
any boats around here?

225
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:42,037
How long will it take
us to reach the shore?

226
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,337
The rest of the night.

227
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:44,300
That's insane!

228
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:47,640
Thanks a lot!

229
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:49,520
Thanks for the ride!

230
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:51,380
Bye, sisters! Oh, shut up!

231
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:53,579
He's the reason we're in this mess!

232
00:13:56,700 --> 00:13:57,740
What the...?

233
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:01,512
It's a Sandoran catfish!

234
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:03,697
They're rarely seen by humans!

235
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:05,486
Doesn't seem that rare to me!

236
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:09,077
Did I mention they love
to eat human flesh?

237
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:11,160
You could've told us a bit sooner!

238
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:21,820
Get off of me, dammit!

239
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:24,317
I can't see a thing with
you hanging on so tight!

240
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:25,230
Chop it!

241
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:34,980
Kong Fu to Kong Fu!

242
00:14:35,420 --> 00:14:38,377
They say they were just looking
out for their fellow pupils.

243
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:39,400
Pupils? What?

244
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:41,177
They think Luffy's our master?

245
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:42,090
Please!

246
00:14:42,173 --> 00:14:43,137
You really want to argue with them?

247
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:44,717
Hang in there, little guys!

248
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,094
Just a little further!

249
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:47,780
Thanks a lot!

250
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:49,300
Bye-bye!

251
00:14:52,420 --> 00:14:55,177
Now that things are going
smoothly, can we make it in time?

252
00:14:55,260 --> 00:14:56,220
I don't know.

253
00:14:56,620 --> 00:14:59,517
Even riding Eyelash, I'm not
sure when we would get there.

254
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:02,577
Not to be pessimistic, but
Eyelash can only carry two of us.

255
00:15:02,660 --> 00:15:05,237
If Baroque Works is gonna attack
us, it'll be from here on.

256
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:06,555
So we can't split up.

257
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:09,287
Isn't there any way for
us to stick together?

258
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:18,540
Look, over there!

259
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:19,840
What is it now?

260
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:20,830
Is it the enemy?

261
00:15:20,913 --> 00:15:23,486
Don't tell me they're
here to kill us already!

262
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:26,920
No, wait! That sound!

263
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:28,870
Karoo!

264
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:32,780
I'm the Supersonic Duck Squadron!

265
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:37,398
You've come to help us, haven't you?

266
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:39,350
Karoo!

267
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:58,220
Come on!

268
00:16:01,220 --> 00:16:03,160
Meat! Meat!

269
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:17,460
We may both be pirates, but you
fall grossly short on skill.

270
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:22,737
This sandstorm will deal Yuba
a final destructive blow,

271
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:27,232
banning the flames of anger within the
rebel army until an inferno ignites.

272
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:35,160
No, no, no!

273
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:16,280
Thank you.

274
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:23,560
Why do you fight?

275
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:31,340
Those of you with the name of D.

276
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:35,090
D...

277
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:38,640
Who are you people?

278
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:40,351
What are your intentions?

279
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:45,594
Apparently you don't have a
clue what I'm talking about.

280
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:52,100
I found you!

281
00:17:57,840 --> 00:17:59,300
Where is Vivi?

282
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:01,230
My...

283
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:03,260
Awake already?

284
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:09,668
Now that I've studied your ability, this
won't turn out like it did last time!

285
00:18:11,060 --> 00:18:12,480
Be careful, pal.

286
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,901
Don't want to overexert yourself.

287
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:22,337
Perfect timing.

288
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:24,891
Why don't you save the boy before he dies?

289
00:18:27,580 --> 00:18:30,992
After all, if it weren't for
his courage and selflessness,

290
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:34,957
who knows if your precious princess
would have made it back alive at all.

291
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:37,440
It must please you to know Vivi's safe.

292
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:40,917
That even as we speak, she's
on her way to Alubarna,

293
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,557
though it's a long trip
and anything could happen.

294
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:45,740
Guess the situation is what it is.

295
00:18:59,700 --> 00:19:02,171
If I'm not able to stop her, then who can?

296
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:05,280
Vivi must be protected
for everyone's sake!

297
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:10,580
Need meat!

298
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:15,860
So, the final revolt has begun.

299
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:17,560
There was a lone ship.

300
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:19,957
Hopefully that means
Princess Vivi and the others

301
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:22,746
were able to make it to
Alabasta in one piece.

302
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:23,900
I must hurry.

303
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:26,129
I pray there's still time.

304
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:30,080
Hey, kid, are you all right?

305
00:19:30,260 --> 00:19:31,240
Need meat.

306
00:19:35,420 --> 00:19:36,250
Meat!

307
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:37,970
Meat?

308
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:39,960
You don't need food now.

309
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:42,077
That's the least of your worries.

310
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:44,219
Hang on, I'll get a doctor for you.

311
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:52,360
I'm going to make sure
Crocodile pays for this.

312
00:19:54,640 --> 00:20:00,100
He insulted Phoebe, and that old
man with this shovel gave me water.

313
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:03,100
He's definitely gonna pay!

314
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:07,160
Who is this person?

315
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:10,320
Meat.

316
00:20:32,620 --> 00:20:33,580
There it is!

317
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:36,466
It's still in the distance,
but it's Alubarna!

318
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:39,640
Koza, we're less than 30 minutes away!

319
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:41,670
Yeah.

320
00:20:41,753 --> 00:20:43,300
We're nearing Alubarna now!

321
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:45,840
The time has come, men!

322
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:53,137
Chaka, we've sighted the Rebel Army.

323
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:55,137
They're about 10 miles to the south.

324
00:20:55,220 --> 00:20:58,777
Their forces are bearing down on
the southern gate as we speak.

325
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:02,340
East, west, south, southeast, southwest.

326
00:21:02,740 --> 00:21:04,564
Guard each gate with your life.

327
00:21:04,820 --> 00:21:09,020
Do not let even one of them set
foot within our walls. Right!

328
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:26,780
Hey, take a look over there.

329
00:21:27,140 --> 00:21:30,740
The rebel army is approaching,
and there are so many of them.

330
00:21:30,980 --> 00:21:34,517
The princess is such a little
idiot to think she can stop them.

331
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:37,071
But then, is the little idiot even coming?

332
00:21:37,320 --> 00:21:38,150
Really?

333
00:21:38,233 --> 00:21:39,097
Now will she show up?

334
00:21:39,180 --> 00:21:40,260
Or will she not?

335
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:41,560
Or will she?

336
00:21:41,860 --> 00:21:42,960
Or will she not?

337
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:44,460
The outcome is vague.

338
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:45,937
What, what, what, what, what?

339
00:21:46,020 --> 00:21:47,297
Are we sure about this?

340
00:21:47,380 --> 00:21:48,297
Shouldn't we be sure?

341
00:21:48,380 --> 00:21:50,697
The princess and the pirates are
really coming right at this break.

342
00:21:50,780 --> 00:21:52,057
The rebel army's gonna beat them here.

343
00:21:52,140 --> 00:21:54,457
I thought those idiots
wanted to stop the fighting!

344
00:21:54,540 --> 00:21:56,217
Shouldn't they at least try to be on time?

345
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:59,297
I think it's entirely possible that
they won't make it soon enough.

346
00:21:59,380 --> 00:22:01,157
It might even be likely, really.

347
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:04,037
After all, they did lose precious
time when they were in Rain Base.

348
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:05,340
What? They did?

349
00:22:05,940 --> 00:22:06,797
All right, then.

350
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:09,357
Let's suppose the rebellion
does get started first.

351
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:12,205
What are we supposed to
do if that does happen?

352
00:22:12,560 --> 00:22:14,977
We wouldn't have to do anything, would we?

353
00:22:15,060 --> 00:22:15,890
Think about it.

354
00:22:15,973 --> 00:22:17,177
Once the rebellion gets underway,

355
00:22:17,260 --> 00:22:19,697
there's nothing even the princess
will be able to do to stop it.

356
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:23,140
All we need to do is eliminate
whoever we're told to.

357
00:22:23,660 --> 00:22:26,637
Can't you even manage to figure
that much out on your own?

358
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:30,117
It sounds like you're just dying
to see some of my dance moves.

359
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:31,517
Just calm down and let it go, you two.

360
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:33,160
Ah! My back! It hurts!

361
00:22:33,380 --> 00:22:34,757
Get over here and massage it, Mr.

362
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:35,670
Four!

363
00:22:35,753 --> 00:22:39,020
You're coming... No!

364
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:40,990
Really?

365
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:43,965
Why didn't you tell us
that earlier, you idiot?

366
00:22:47,980 --> 00:22:48,810
Ducks!

367
00:22:48,893 --> 00:22:49,723
They're on ducks!

368
00:22:50,520 --> 00:22:52,840
They're on ducks. Are you sure?

369
00:22:53,040 --> 00:22:54,511
Do you see anything else?

370
00:22:54,860 --> 00:22:56,637
Seems like their number's gone up, too!

371
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:57,937
There are six of them!

372
00:22:58,020 --> 00:23:02,785
With Straw Hat out of the way, I thought
there was only supposed to be four left!

373
00:23:02,940 --> 00:23:04,517
Not quite, Miss Merry Christmas.

374
00:23:04,600 --> 00:23:06,277
Don't you remember what the boss said?

375
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:07,948
He told us there's that Mr.

376
00:23:08,060 --> 00:23:09,001
Prince guy, too.

377
00:23:09,100 --> 00:23:12,517
And apparently there's more than one
of them, so the numbers do add up.

378
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:13,600
Just do the math.

379
00:23:14,580 --> 00:23:15,737
It doesn't matter.

380
00:23:15,820 --> 00:23:17,349
Phoebe is our only target.

381
00:23:19,140 --> 00:23:19,970
it.

382
00:23:20,053 --> 00:23:20,957
What are you so worried about?

383
00:23:21,040 --> 00:23:22,020
Well, Mr.

384
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:26,100
One, you say Princess Vivi
is the only one we need to

385
00:23:30,020 --> 00:23:30,850
eliminate?

386
00:23:30,933 --> 00:23:31,763
Okay.

387
00:23:31,846 --> 00:23:34,017
Then how about you take a stab
at guessing which one she is?

388
00:23:34,100 --> 00:23:35,218
They're all wearing

389
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:39,177
identical outfits!

390
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:42,017
Even worse, those birds are the
quickest in the whole kingdom.

391
00:23:42,100 --> 00:23:43,100
Supersonic ducks.

392
00:23:48,060 --> 00:23:49,560
You sneaky rats!

393
00:23:49,880 --> 00:23:53,217
How are we supposed to tell
which one is Phoebe like this?

394
00:23:53,300 --> 00:23:55,920
It's just not a fair
thing to do, you know!

395
00:24:05,860 --> 00:24:07,980
Let them have it down, Mr. Four!

396
00:24:12,020 --> 00:24:12,900
Dodge it!

397
00:24:16,180 --> 00:24:18,980
Miss him, those damn
birds, they're too fast.

398
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:22,437
Two just broke off from the rest.

399
00:24:22,520 --> 00:24:23,697
They're splitting up.

400
00:24:23,780 --> 00:24:26,097
Looks like they're planning
to go for the south gate.

401
00:24:26,180 --> 00:24:28,957
Those two are heading straight
toward the rebel army.

402
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:31,280
Which means one of them must be Vivi.

403
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:33,917
We'll go ahead and take care of those two.

404
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:35,200
Move it, Mr.

405
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:36,170
Four

406
00:24:39,460 --> 00:24:41,480
Special attack, firestorm

407
00:24:45,180 --> 00:24:47,677
Two more of them are
breaking off that way, Mr.

408
00:24:47,760 --> 00:24:48,590
One!

409
00:24:48,673 --> 00:24:49,503
That could be Mimi!

410
00:24:49,640 --> 00:24:52,497
Seems they're planning to
go in through the West Gate.

411
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:53,540
Damn brats.

412
00:24:54,420 --> 00:24:55,250
Let's go.

413
00:24:59,500 --> 00:25:00,330
Okay!

414
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:02,675
Let's head for the Southwest Gate now!

415
00:25:05,520 --> 00:25:09,873
So they're going to approach three of
Alibarna's five gates from the West.

416
00:25:10,020 --> 00:25:13,057
If they're gonna split up and enter
that way, then we'll do the same thing.

417
00:25:13,140 --> 00:25:15,316
We can wipe them out inside the city.

418
00:25:16,180 --> 00:25:18,062
You're not getting away from me!

419
00:25:23,340 --> 00:25:24,634
Hey, someone's coming!

420
00:25:24,880 --> 00:25:25,880
Is it the Rebels?

421
00:25:26,100 --> 00:25:26,960
No, wait!

422
00:25:27,640 --> 00:25:29,640
It's the Supersonic Duck Squadron!

423
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:30,590
Let them in!

424
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:44,790
Oh!

425
00:25:45,140 --> 00:25:46,800
I'm not kidding here!

426
00:25:46,980 --> 00:25:49,627
There's no way you're
getting away with this!

427
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:53,760
Hair! Hair! Hair! Hair!

428
00:26:02,580 --> 00:26:03,410
Teeheehee!

429
00:26:03,660 --> 00:26:06,637
Thank you so much for
following us all the way here!

430
00:26:06,720 --> 00:26:07,660
Say what?

431
00:26:11,660 --> 00:26:12,597
Now stop?

432
00:26:12,680 --> 00:26:15,557
Wow you guys are very good!

433
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:16,937
You know that's right!

434
00:26:17,020 --> 00:26:18,097
I'm the real princess!

435
00:26:18,180 --> 00:26:19,010
Bb What are you?

436
00:26:19,093 --> 00:26:20,957
I mean what are you talking about?

437
00:26:21,040 --> 00:26:22,737
I am the real princess!

438
00:26:22,820 --> 00:26:23,650
Bb

439
00:26:26,080 --> 00:26:28,640
I wonder if this is far enough now?

440
00:26:32,900 --> 00:26:35,037
I have to say it's really entertaining!

441
00:26:35,120 --> 00:26:36,977
How easily you all fell for this!

442
00:26:37,060 --> 00:26:41,060
Now, we can go ahead and take
these silly cloaks along.

443
00:26:42,720 --> 00:26:43,550
Too bad!

444
00:26:43,660 --> 00:26:45,719
It looks like your guess was wrong!

445
00:26:50,940 --> 00:26:51,770
Wado?!

446
00:26:57,800 --> 00:26:59,820
Thank you so much, everyone.

447
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:03,320
I have to hurry now.

448
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:05,776
The rebel army is almost to the city.

449
00:27:07,380 --> 00:27:08,600
Let's go, Kaido.

450
00:27:10,860 --> 00:27:11,690
Camel!

451
00:27:12,280 --> 00:27:16,020
And I recognize you from the
ship, too, don't I? Saru!

452
00:27:17,280 --> 00:27:18,540
Yeah, come on, Zoro!

453
00:27:18,640 --> 00:27:19,470
Let him have it!

454
00:27:19,553 --> 00:27:21,017
Would you keep quiet over there?

455
00:27:21,100 --> 00:27:22,520
They fooled us.

456
00:27:22,960 --> 00:27:23,817
Quite a farce.

457
00:27:23,900 --> 00:27:24,777
I don't know that anymore!

458
00:27:24,860 --> 00:27:25,742
You cleared me!

459
00:27:26,300 --> 00:27:29,065
It looks like there won't
be any rebellion now.

460
00:27:29,460 --> 00:27:30,540
What did you say?

461
00:27:33,880 --> 00:27:35,957
I have to stop them at any cost.

462
00:27:36,040 --> 00:27:39,628
If I don't, then all of this
struggling has been for nothing.

463
00:27:40,700 --> 00:27:41,880
Whatever the cost,

464
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:46,807
Vivi and her friends must be prevented
from making contact with the rebel army.

465
00:27:53,800 --> 00:27:55,240
Secure the cannonballs!

466
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:57,237
I don't want them rolling away!

467
00:27:57,320 --> 00:27:58,438
You heard him, men!

468
00:27:58,600 --> 00:27:59,620
Man your posts!

469
00:27:59,860 --> 00:28:01,801
Keep the artillery under control!

470
00:28:02,500 --> 00:28:04,441
The ground is really moving, huh?

471
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:07,960
The enemy army is made up
of two million angry men.

472
00:28:08,160 --> 00:28:10,037
Even the ground shakes
a little bit for them.

473
00:28:10,120 --> 00:28:10,950
Stay strong.

474
00:28:22,500 --> 00:28:23,700
It's okay, Karoo.

475
00:28:23,820 --> 00:28:25,349
You don't have to be here.

476
00:28:28,300 --> 00:28:30,829
You could get trampled,
so just be careful.

477
00:28:42,440 --> 00:28:45,620
Please, leader, please
listen to what I have to say.

478
00:28:45,880 --> 00:28:46,900
You must hear it.

479
00:28:52,700 --> 00:28:53,820
Everyone listen!

480
00:28:54,120 --> 00:28:56,117
Close your ranks and stay together!

481
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:58,617
We'll knock through the
guards at the southern gate!

482
00:28:58,700 --> 00:29:00,465
The rest will fall from there!

483
00:29:01,060 --> 00:29:03,120
Do not lose arms!

484
00:29:11,320 --> 00:29:13,200
Rebel Army, you must stop!

485
00:29:13,660 --> 00:29:16,189
This fight is pointless, it's all a Step!

486
00:29:19,640 --> 00:29:22,580
Please slow down, you
have got to listen to me!

487
00:29:27,380 --> 00:29:29,020
Rebel Army, stop!

488
00:29:34,400 --> 00:29:37,717
Hey, did you see a person
standing in front of us just now?

489
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:38,630
Person?

490
00:29:38,713 --> 00:29:40,357
That isn't important right now.

491
00:29:40,440 --> 00:29:42,558
The enemy is already shooting at us.

492
00:29:46,560 --> 00:29:47,880
Why did they do that?

493
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:50,160
Neither side can see anything now.

494
00:29:52,700 --> 00:29:54,582
What is the Royal Army thinking?

495
00:29:56,480 --> 00:29:57,540
What the hell?

496
00:29:57,780 --> 00:30:00,477
I haven't given anyone
the order to open fire.

497
00:30:00,560 --> 00:30:02,177
Do not act without my Zeus.

498
00:30:02,260 --> 00:30:04,700
Uh, sir, I'm terribly sorry about that.

499
00:30:04,900 --> 00:30:07,320
I guess my hand just slipped. Sorry.

500
00:30:27,860 --> 00:30:29,960
Don't back down! Charge through!

501
00:30:30,220 --> 00:30:31,749
It's such a cloud of sand!

502
00:30:32,260 --> 00:30:33,090
No, everyone!

503
00:30:33,200 --> 00:30:34,435
You have to stop now!

504
00:30:35,420 --> 00:30:36,800
Fight for the country!

505
00:30:37,080 --> 00:30:38,500
We'll make the king pay!

506
00:30:39,620 --> 00:30:40,450
Leader!

507
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:51,390
Leader!

508
00:31:00,320 --> 00:31:01,580
Koza, what is it?

509
00:31:02,260 --> 00:31:03,720
Nothing! It's nothing!

510
00:31:05,760 --> 00:31:07,280
Was I imagining it?

511
00:31:21,360 --> 00:31:22,190
Leader?

512
00:31:25,260 --> 00:31:26,090
Remember a bit!

513
00:31:26,173 --> 00:31:28,020
Today will be our final battle!

514
00:31:30,020 --> 00:31:31,020
Wait!

515
00:31:31,200 --> 00:31:32,080
Listen to me!

516
00:31:34,580 --> 00:31:35,580
Wait!

517
00:31:52,980 --> 00:31:54,377
They're here!

518
00:31:54,460 --> 00:31:57,080
Get it ready!

519
00:32:02,740 --> 00:32:03,570
Fire!

520
00:32:24,460 --> 00:32:25,900
Save the country!

521
00:32:26,180 --> 00:32:27,700
Tare down Autobahna!

522
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:01,580
No, Karoo!

523
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:08,280
Karoo, you shielded me from them.

524
00:33:11,240 --> 00:33:12,520
I'm sorry.

525
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:14,800
We've come so far.

526
00:33:15,080 --> 00:33:16,720
We've done so much.

527
00:33:17,520 --> 00:33:19,537
But the rebellion has started.

528
00:33:19,620 --> 00:33:22,677
I'm so sorry, but I will stop it.

529
00:33:22,760 --> 00:33:27,701
No matter how many times they refuse to
listen, no matter how loudly I have to yell,

530
00:33:28,160 --> 00:33:32,177
we will not let mindless fighting
destroy what we've worked so hard for.

531
00:33:32,260 --> 00:33:35,613
That's something I learned
while I was on board the ship.

532
00:33:36,020 --> 00:33:37,700
Do not ever give up!

533
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:41,470
Phoebe!

534
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:44,960
At last, I found you!

535
00:33:45,600 --> 00:33:46,430
Usopp!

536
00:33:46,620 --> 00:33:48,500
We can still make it in time!

537
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:50,380
Hurry and hop on! Right.

538
00:33:50,860 --> 00:33:51,877
Hang in there, Karoo.

539
00:33:51,960 --> 00:33:53,940
Oh, forget about that bird.

540
00:33:56,020 --> 00:33:57,217
What's the matter, Vivi?

541
00:33:57,300 --> 00:33:59,177
Come on, we need to get going now.

542
00:33:59,260 --> 00:34:00,090
Hurry it up!

543
00:34:04,420 --> 00:34:05,380
That bird?

544
00:34:09,940 --> 00:34:11,240
Let's go, Karoo!

545
00:34:16,120 --> 00:34:19,040
Come on, the rebellion
will only get worse.

546
00:34:23,800 --> 00:34:25,140
Usopp, prove yourself.

547
00:34:26,460 --> 00:34:27,420
Hmm? Really?

548
00:34:27,680 --> 00:34:29,504
You don't believe that it's me?

549
00:34:31,380 --> 00:34:32,210
See?

550
00:34:32,580 --> 00:34:33,410
No!

551
00:34:35,800 --> 00:34:36,630
Usopp.

552
00:34:36,713 --> 00:34:37,543
Hey, Usopp.

553
00:34:37,820 --> 00:34:38,880
Eyelash, wake up.

554
00:34:40,220 --> 00:34:41,480
Oh, it's you, Sanji.

555
00:34:41,680 --> 00:34:42,974
Is it morning already?

556
00:34:43,120 --> 00:34:44,160
Uh, sure.

557
00:34:44,400 --> 00:34:46,517
So, this is how our fight turned out.

558
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:49,317
The part of the mission where we
lured them away went really well.

559
00:34:49,400 --> 00:34:54,280
But then, well, you see, then
it was over in two seconds.

560
00:34:54,740 --> 00:34:55,681
One second each.

561
00:34:56,240 --> 00:34:58,240
You couldn't have held out longer?

562
00:34:59,700 --> 00:35:01,524
What are you doing here anyway?

563
00:35:01,940 --> 00:35:03,320
Your ducks got me.

564
00:35:03,420 --> 00:35:04,837
They came to get some help for you two.

565
00:35:04,920 --> 00:35:07,060
But that aside, you let Mr.

566
00:35:07,160 --> 00:35:09,340
Two get away, didn't you? Yeah.

567
00:35:14,740 --> 00:35:15,570
Listen up.

568
00:35:15,760 --> 00:35:18,137
That creepy ballerina's
transformations are perfect.

569
00:35:18,220 --> 00:35:20,077
There's no telling when he might pose as

570
00:35:20,160 --> 00:35:22,137
one of us and make an
attempt on Vivi's life.

571
00:35:22,220 --> 00:35:23,691
Does everyone understand?

572
00:35:24,240 --> 00:35:27,358
If you ever feel like one
of us is acting suspicious,

573
00:35:29,540 --> 00:35:32,397
ask them to take off this
wrapping and reveal their mark.

574
00:35:32,480 --> 00:35:35,009
If they can't do that,
they're an imposter.

575
00:35:35,580 --> 00:35:36,410
Whoa.

576
00:35:36,493 --> 00:35:37,577
Having such a well-thought-out plan like

577
00:35:37,660 --> 00:35:40,337
this seems uncharacteristically
smart for you.

578
00:35:40,420 --> 00:35:43,437
So how can we be sure you
aren't already an imposter?

579
00:35:43,520 --> 00:35:44,420
I'll stab you!

580
00:35:44,740 --> 00:35:45,820
Yeah, that's him.

581
00:35:46,500 --> 00:35:48,140
Ooh, definitely Zoro.

582
00:35:54,340 --> 00:35:55,380
You're lying.

583
00:35:56,120 --> 00:35:57,780
You're not really Usopp.

584
00:35:59,340 --> 00:36:01,480
Well, that's too bad.

585
00:36:02,900 --> 00:36:04,060
No, really.

586
00:36:04,380 --> 00:36:05,880
You knew how.

587
00:36:06,520 --> 00:36:09,100
I thought my imitation was perfect.

588
00:36:10,020 --> 00:36:12,397
We even had a helpful
report from the boss?

589
00:36:12,480 --> 00:36:13,837
That you all had the same bandages.

590
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:15,737
wrapped up on your arm like this.

591
00:36:15,820 --> 00:36:17,000
So smart of you!

592
00:36:18,360 --> 00:36:19,820
This isn't good.

593
00:36:21,840 --> 00:36:23,040
Phoebe's in danger!
